Notebook[{
Cell["Hypergraph Rewriting", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"d6bed0bb-b93b-8e42-b949-0906431d2eb4"],

Cell["WolframInstitute`Hypergraphs` \[LongDash] rules, matches and events", \
"Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"bfb1b821-daf5-ba42-a680-53e46fbdf2c4"],

Cell["\<\
A rewrite rule is a pair of hypergraphs. Applying it to a hypergraph means \
finding the ways its input sits inside that hypergraph, and for each of them \
replacing what was matched by the output. This notebook is the tour of that: \
what a rule is, how matching works and what it depends on, and what an \
application gives back. Everything below is live output from src/.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5b7d1f06-3a74-db46-8b87-be6bbbc48a84"],

Cell["\<\
The machinery around rewriting \[LongDash] the generations of states a rule \
produces, the causal graph of its events, the conditions under which two \
events depend on one another \[LongDash] is built on top of this, out of the \
events described in section 3. It is in CausalityBasics.nb.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5f417a72-4e6b-c247-8b92-8902cf47f782"],

Cell["Loading the package", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9b450f21-e48a-134d-a8d1-b1423e906bea"],

Cell["\<\
The cell below is an initialization cell, which the front end evaluates when \
this notebook is opened. By the time you read this the package is already \
loaded.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e1eab2ba-742d-194b-b499-f870e6b02ed6"],

Cell["\<\
PacletDirectoryLoad[ParentDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]]];
Needs[\"WolframInstitute`Hypergraphs`\"]\
\>", "Input",
 InitializationCell->
  True,ExpressionUUID->"d50f4f85-ff71-be46-976a-1888ff9b414a"],

Cell["1. A rule is a pair of hypergraphs", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a6b70e0c-878a-0447-965a-bd6ae10ec14e"],

Cell["\<\
HypergraphRule takes an input and an output. Either may be written as \
anything Hypergraph accepts, so a rule can be given as plainly as a pair of \
edge lists:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8679d886-f7ec-a345-b756-3cc0b87072d7"],

Cell["sub = HypergraphRule[{{1, 2}}, {{1, 3}, {3, 2}}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"75be68c1-40f6-4c40-b07a-be926e572bb8"],

