594a-bca2-2d6e5c12a6da"],

Cell["HypergraphRuleMatches[sub, chain]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"134b3040-7608-1547-a757-1af518db954d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\<\"MatchEdgePositions\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"RuleVertexMap\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"1", "\[Rule]", "1"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"2", "\[Rule]", "2"}]}], "\[RightAssociation]"}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"LabelBindings\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", "\[RightAssociation]"}]}]}], 
    "\[RightAssociation]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\<\"MatchEdgePositions\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"RuleVertexMap\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"1", "\[Rule]", "2"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"2", "\[Rule]", "3"}]}], "\[RightAssociation]"}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"LabelBindings\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", "\[RightAssociation]"}]}]}], 
    "\[RightAssociation]"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"96d2f4c2-\
9a6f-7c4b-b02a-3d0795493d5b"],

Cell["\<\
Two matches, because the single edge of the input can lie on either edge of \
the chain. Each match says which positions of EdgeList it used and how the \
input's vertices correspond to the hypergraph's.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"efbe3752-dbb9-a247-bb47-868749c2e67a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Design note.  ",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "Asking for the matches without rewriting is the way to see why a rule \
applies as often as it does. When a rule produces more events than expected, \
it is almost always the matching that is surprising rather than the rewriting."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{2, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameMargins->{{10, 0}, {6, 6}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.7],
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.25],ExpressionUUID->"29946c41-2f22-1a4d-9f76-5f5d35d70b4a"],

Cell["Symmetry decides how many ways a pattern fits", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"6b2aa84f-4d0b-4245-b4f2-2900a48a5026"],

Cell["\<\
A pattern edge and the edge it lies on must have the same symmetry type, and \
the pattern is matched over the orderings that type allows. A directed edge \
of arity three fits one way, a cyclic one three ways, an unordered one all \
six:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b183cf07-ccc4-ac49-bc67-8837a8b59ee2"],

Cell["\<\
Table[
  Length @ HypergraphRuleMatches[
    HypergraphRule[{Edge[{1, 2, 3}, s]}, {}], Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2, 3}, \
s]}]],
  {s, {\"Directed\", \"Cyclic\", \"Unordered\"}}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9026e393-2348-8843-bb11-1f2cb5306d38"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"1", ",", "3", ",", "6"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->\
"21765e63-a12f-694a-b019-0365f4132110"],

Cell["\<\
And the types have to agree, so a directed pattern finds nothing in an \
unordered edge:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"26ffd4b8-ea6e-3f4a-a5d9-086147953c9c"],

Cell["\<\
HypergraphRuleMatches[HypergraphRule[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\"]}, {}],
  Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"]}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"455734da-29f6-ca41-8449-41b3885df355"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"61aff74e-3c33-764c-bb44-891153b9628c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Design note.  ",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "Those six matches of an unordered triple are genuinely six, not one \
reported six times: they differ in which vertex of the hypergraph each vertex \
of the rule corresponds to, and an output that treats its vertices \
differently will produce six different results. When the output is symmetric \
too, the six results coincide, and the multiplicity is then something to \
divide out rather than something wrong."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{2, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameMargins->{{10, 0}, {6, 6}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.7],
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.25],ExpressionUUID->"f6bbc067-5ef4-1443-82ba-09ccd4300688"],

Cell["Two vertices of a rule do not fold onto one", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"1cb84cc4-beba-1c41-aa82-4fb1afc39efc"],

Cell["\<\
By default distinct vertices of the input match distinct vertices of the \
hypergraph, so a two-vertex pattern does not fit a self-loop:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d3354461-ea3c-4e4f-8237-f6ee45b2fe9a"],

Cell["\<\
{HypergraphRuleMatches[HypergraphRule[{{1, 2}}, {}], Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, \
1}]}]],
  Length @ HypergraphRuleMatches[HypergraphRule[{{1, 2}}, {}], \
Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 1}]}],
     \"DistinctVertices\" -> False]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"110d3269-500c-0d4e-a60c-0d2f90e3971d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", "1"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"1224e262-\
2ebd-1044-8391-a561a46b83e1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Design note.  ",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "This follows the reference paclet, which imposes the same by default. It is \
worth knowing that it is a choice: in the Wolfram model a rule's vertices \
need not be distinct, and \"DistinctVertices\" -> False is that convention."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{2, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameMargins->{{10, 0}, {6, 6}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.7],
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.25],ExpressionUUID->"5b258cb4-d2e3-9642-ab8f-cc46d586130b"],

Cell["An edge is used once", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"0f5d3db0-1679-dc41-89d0-214201ff5c5e"],

Cell["\<\
Each edge of the hypergraph is used by at most one edge of the input, so a \
rule wanting two edges wants two of them:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"350a3b15-fbd8-d04b-a5c5-7e4e5490a594"],

Cell["\<\
{HypergraphRuleMatches[HypergraphRule[{{1, 2}, {1, 2}}, {}], \
Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}]}]],
  Length @ HypergraphRuleMatches[HypergraphRule[{{1, 2}, {1, 2}}, {}],
     Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}], Edge[{1, 2}]}]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"d9aec314-1b67-1640-816e-cca1bbe15bbb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", "2"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"b4cdfad0-\
0e25-464c-b2ea-521d21e26729"],

Cell["3. Applying a rule: events", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"174eae98-b199-e345-9b24-7a91ea34c957"],

Cell["\<\
Applying a rule gives one event for every match. An event is an association: \
it says what the hypergraph became, and also what was matched, what was \
created and what was destroyed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ea6e226e-9ad1-0f4a-800d-dc2bde01c199"],

Cell["\<\
events = sub[chain];
Length[events]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"cc689baf-56e1-d24c-8337-70d5bec65cc3"],

Cell[BoxData["2"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"52548486-8ed9-5240-9132-88dfe26c4f5e"],

Cell["Keys @ First[events]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"2a6510cb-1208-8140-94da-586db360c8b6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"Hypergraph\"\>", ",", "\<\"EdgeOrigins\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"MatchVertices\"\>", ",", "\<\"MatchEdges\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"MatchEdgePositions\"\>", ",", "\<\"NewVertices\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"NewEdges\"\>", ",", "\<\"DeletedVertices\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"RuleVertexMap\"\>", ",", "\<\"LabelBindings\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"Rule\"\>"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"e6a97680-faef-\
6b4d-801b-b63ecc0d1f5b"],

Cell["\<\
The two results, drawn. Each has subdivided one of the two edges:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"16fd4713-ca23-cf45-8a5c-4ed3d105dc69"],

Cell["#[\"Hypergraph\"] & /@ events", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"4a5ecdf5-4846-b240-b4af-b4ee01f812a8"],

