Cell["\<\
Three events, one per edge. They are distinct as events but isomorphic as \
hypergraphs, which CanonicalHypergraph makes plain:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"df10970e-214e-8f4e-9303-993e169d8cca"],

Cell["\<\
Length @ DeleteDuplicates[CanonicalHypergraph[#[\"Hypergraph\"]] & /@ \
sub[star]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"62c7c5e5-d2fc-c84c-8f62-5db38f1b1ca0"],

Cell[BoxData["1"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"90043e1b-2fe3-0146-8761-ac29108fd4a1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Design note.  ",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "Distinct events with isomorphic results is the ordinary situation, not a \
special case, and it is why a multiway system has to decide whether its \
states are hypergraphs or isomorphism classes of them. The pieces for either \
reading are already here."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{2, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameMargins->{{10, 0}, {6, 6}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.7],
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.25],ExpressionUUID->"a888ce6c-fd11-7f41-b2d6-3e2f3bbdd894"],

Cell["An unordered rule", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"80945b5e-c208-f843-9f70-9a95d4007872"],

Cell["\<\
Nothing about rewriting is particular to directed edges. Here an unordered \
pair becomes an unordered triple:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"45fa327e-315c-6e43-9ce7-43fc57e59e39"],

Cell["\<\
grow = HypergraphRule[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"]},
                      {Edge[{1, 2, 3}, \"Unordered\"]}];
Length @ grow[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"]}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"936cdecf-e7a4-5245-8358-2ac2147e38d0"],

Cell[BoxData["2"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"3d6f6318-6848-df4a-8067-8cc84ad30b2f"],

Cell["\<\
Two events, from the two orderings the unordered pattern admits, and their \
results are the same hypergraph:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"90db6566-66b5-3a46-b45d-926dd4915e36"],

Cell["\<\
DeleteDuplicates[#[\"Hypergraph\"] & /@ grow[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \
\"Unordered\"]}]]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ca5af552-8914-6f4f-8599-ba83b043319a"],

